window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["tr-22.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">الشرح الأصلي بالإنكليزية.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> ابحث بالرمز أو بالاسم الإنكليزي. تأكد من نوع ناقل الحركة بسيارتك قبل ما تتبع دليل معيّن.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">P = نقل الحركة: 62</span><span class=\"en-chip\">U = اتصال الشبكة: 31</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">93 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d95-00 tcm clutch failure undetermined\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D95-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM CLUTCH FAILURE UNDETERMINED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC)s set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. TCM will inhibit Transmission from being shifted out of PARK. Reverse will be disabled. Drive will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d96-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a or b defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D96-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A OR B DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC)s set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record the Event and Environmental Data on the repair order as it may be needed to determine the root cause of this DTC. It may be very difficult to reset this DTC so this step is very important .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC. Pay particular attention to the shifts relating to this DTC. If rough shifting is present and the Adaptation Procedure has been performed. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d97-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a or d defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D97-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A OR D DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d98-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch b or d defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D98-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH B OR D DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d99-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch b or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D99-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH B OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record the Event and Environmental Data on the repair order as it may be needed to determine the root cause of this DTC. It may be very difficult to reset this DTC so this step is very important .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC. Pay particular attention to the shifts relating to this DTC. If rough shifting is present and the Adaptation Procedure has been performed. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d9a-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch c or d defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D9A-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH C OR D DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d9b-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D9B-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d9c-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a or c defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D9C-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A OR C DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d9d-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch b or c defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D9D-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH B OR C DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d9e-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch c or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D9E-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH C OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1d9f-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch d or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1D9F-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH D OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da0-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a b or c defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA0-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A B OR C DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da1-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a b or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA1-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A B OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da2-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch b c or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA2-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH B C OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da3-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch b d or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA3-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH B D OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da4-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch b c or d defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA4-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH B C OR D DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da5-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch c d or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA5-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH C D OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da6-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a c or d defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA6-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A C OR D DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da7-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a d or e defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA7-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A D OR E DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da8-00 incorrect gear ratio clutch a b or d defective\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA8-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO CLUTCH A B OR D DEFECTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fixed gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</li><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the Transmission fluid is at the proper level before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record the Event and Environmental Data on the repair order as it may be needed to determine the root cause of this DTC. It may be very difficult to reset this DTC so this step is very important .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid condition.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission fluid burnt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC. Pay particular attention to the shifts relating to this DTC. If rough shifting is present and the Adaptation Procedure has been performed. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Valve Body in accordance with the Service information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1da9-00 transmission fluid temperature rationality\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DA9-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TRANSMISSION FLUID TEMPERATURE RATIONALITY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The transmission monitoring system uses three temperature sensors. If any one of the sensors fail, the other two sensors are used for the control and temperature monitoring calculations and the Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) will not be illuminated. The MIL will only illuminate when more than one temperature sensor has a failure.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       If only one of the temperature sensors has failed and the MIL is not illuminated, do not perform any temperature sensor related repairs. The TCM will use the other two sensors to calculate the proper transmission operation.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">One of the sensors is located in the oil sump of the transmission and can be monitored with a scan tool under the Oil Temperature Sensor data parameter. This sensor is a 2-wire thermistor with a negative temperature coefficient. This means that as the temperature increases, the resistance of the sensor decreases.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The other two sensors are embedded on the Printed Circuit Board (PCB) in two separate areas of the Transmission Control Module (TCM). The TCM is attached to the valve body and therefore provides the three sensors with a strong temperature correlation. The embedded sensors can not be monitored with the scan tool and cannot be serviced separately.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The oil temperature sensor that is located in the oil sump is normally used exclusively for the transmission control calculations. The embedded sensors located in the TCM are normally used for over-temperature shutdown and temperature sensor rationality monitoring. The following table shows the relationship between temperature and resistance of the Oil Temperature Sensor located in the oil sump.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                               TEMPERATURE vs RESISTANCE\n                  TEMPERATURE                             RESISTANCE\n                  -30°C (-22°F)                     37, 400 - 50, 600 Ohms\n                   10°C (50°F)                       5, 810 - 7, 100 Ohms\n                  110°C (230°F)                         231 - 263 Ohms\n                  145°C (293°F)                         105 - 117 Ohms</pre></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Engine speed received via CAN message or Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A malfunction is detected on more than one of the three temperature sensors.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MIL is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RESTRICTION IN TRANSMISSION COOLING SYSTEM</li><li>INCORRECT FLUID LEVEL</li><li>VEHICLE AIRFLOW RESTRICTED</li><li>TORQUE CONVERTER</li><li>CASE VENT PLUGGED OR DAMAGED</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR RELATED TRANSMISSION TEMPERATURE SENSOR DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any other Transmission Temperature Sensor DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair Temperature Sensor DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1daa-00 trans temp undetermined\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DAA-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TRANS TEMP UNDETERMINED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The transmission monitoring system uses three temperature sensors. If any one of the sensors fail, the other two sensors are used for the control and temperature monitoring calculations and the Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) will not be illuminated. The MIL will only illuminate when more than one temperature sensor has a failure.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        If only one of the temperature sensors has failed and the MIL is not illuminated, do not perform any temperature sensor related repairs. The TCM will use the other two sensors to calculate the proper transmission operation.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">One of the sensors is located in the oil sump of the transmission and can be monitored with a scan tool under the Oil Temperature Sensor data parameter. This sensor is a 2-wire thermistor with a negative temperature coefficient. This means that as the temperature increases, the resistance of the sensor decreases.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The other two sensors are embedded on the Printed Circuit Board (PCB) in two separate areas of the Transmission Control Module (TCM). The TCM is attached to the valve body and therefore provides the three sensors with a strong temperature correlation. The embedded sensors can not be monitored with the scan tool and cannot be serviced separately.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The oil temperature sensor that is located in the oil sump is normally used exclusively for the transmission control calculations. The embedded sensors located in the TCM are normally used for over-temperature shutdown and temperature sensor rationality monitoring. The following table shows the relationship between temperature and resistance of the Oil Temperature Sensor located in the oil sump.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                               TEMPERATURE vs RESISTANCE\n                  TEMPERATURE                             RESISTANCE\n                  -30°C (-22°F)                     37, 400 - 50, 600 Ohms\n                   10°C (50°F)                       5, 810 - 7, 100 Ohms\n                  110°C (230°F)                         231 - 263 Ohms\n                  145°C (293°F)                         105 - 117 Ohms</pre></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Engine speed received via Controller Area Network (CAN) message or Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A malfunction is detected on more than one of the three temperature sensors.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via CAN. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION FLUID TEMPERATURE SENSOR DTC SET</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION FLUID TEMPERATURE SENSOR DTCS</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any Transmission Temperature Sensor DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair Transmission Temperature Sensor DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dab-00 vehicle speed undetermined\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DAB-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">VEHICLE SPEED UNDETERMINED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic is a continuous test that monitors the Vehicle Speed Sensor (VSS) for lack of activity. The test will not run if a limp-in condition exists for the Manifold Absolute Temperature (MAP), Throttle Position, or Engine Coolant Temperature. If the VSS signal is below a calibrated value for a period of time after the vehicle is operated at a sufficient load, a Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will set.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine speed above 1, 500 rpm. Shifter is not in PARK or NEUTRAL. Brakes are not applied.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">No vehicle speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal is received from the Antilock Brake System (ABS) Module within 300ms.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via CAN. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ACTIVE BUS OR COMMUNICATION DTCS PRESENT</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Diagnose communication DTCs before proceeding. If no communication DTCs are set, diagnose Antilock Brake System (ABS) DTCs before proceeding.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This DTC can set due to differences in tire diameter. Check tire diameters to make sure the tires are the same size.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This DTC can set due to wheel spin.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>VISUAL INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC can set due to differences in tire diameter.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC may set on a hard acceleration on loose gravel or during other off road driving conditions.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check all of the tires for the correct pressure.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check tire wear on all the tires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check that all tire sizes are the same.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Ask the customer what the road and driving conditions were like when the fault set.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary. If the DTC set during a front or rear wheel spin condition, no repair is necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to for 3.6L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST , for 5.7L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST , for 6.2L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST , for 6.4L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Speed Sensors, ABS Module, and the PCM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Vehicle Speed Sensors, ABS Module, and PCM connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. for 3.6L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST , for 5.7L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST , for 6.2L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST , for 6.4L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the PCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. for 3.6L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST , for 5.7L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST , for 6.2L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">TEST , for 6.4L engines. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dac-00 engine speed undetermined\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DAC-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ENGINE SPEED UNDETERMINED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic monitors for a double failure of the Engine Speed signal received via Controller Area Network (CAN) and an electrical or rationality failure of the Input Speed Sensor. If the Transmission Control Module (TCM) detects a failure with both tests this Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will set.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs one time during an ignition cycle.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A failure with the Engine Speed signal received via Controller Area Network (CAN) and an electrical or rationality failure of the Input Speed sensor is present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via CAN. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS ARE SET</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK THE POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, check the PCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. Check Service Bulletins for possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Were any of the above described problems found ?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the condition found above.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If no problems are found, replace and program the PCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dad-00 input shaft-output shaft direction correlation\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DAD-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INPUT SHAFT-OUTPUT SHAFT DIRECTION CORRELATION</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to detect an unwanted driving direction. A rationality check is performed between the measured directions of input speed and output speed signal and the calculated driving direction. The calculated driving direction is based on the commanded currents of the pressure regulators.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No Input Speed Sensor or Output Speed Sensor Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal and Output Speed Sensor signal above a calibrated value. Shift not in progress. No clutch slip control function active.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The failure is detected if the measured directions of input speed and output speed signal do not correspond to the calculated driving direction for a calibrated amount of time. When Calculated Driving Direction is Forward: The measured directions of input speed and output speed signal do not correspond to the calculated driving direction for a calibrated amount of time. When Calculated Driving Direction is Reverse: A failure is detected if the input speed and output speed direction are the same.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via Controller Area Network (CAN). Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Raise the vehicle on the hoist.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor the Output Speed Sensor rpm.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Firmly apply the brakes and place the gear selector in Drive.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        To avoid personal injury or death, keep hands and feet clear of rotating wheels.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Release the brakes and raise the engine speed to allow the Transmission to upshift to the 1-2 and 2-3 shift schedule.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the Output Speed Sensor display an rpm below 1, 000?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FOR INTERNAL FAILURE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This DTC is an indication of a internal Transmission failure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the Transmission Oil Pan and inspect for excessive debris such as clutch friction material or metal contamination.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any indication of an internal Transmission failure?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair internal Transmission as necessary in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to DISASSEMBLY .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dae-00 position valve stuck 2nd gear trans limp in\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DAE-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">POSITION VALVE STUCK 2ND GEAR TRANS LIMP IN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of this Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is to detect a condition where the solenoid controlled Position Valve is stuck in the wrong position. The purpose of the Position Valve is to control the oil supply to the clutches and the parking lock. If the Position Valve is in the wrong position at engine start up, the Parking Lock will be disengaged. This Diagnostic runs once at engine startup.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No engine speed Controller Area Network (CAN) Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Engine has been off for a calibrated amount of time. Park Lock Sensor indicates an engaged park lock at ignition on before the Engine is restarted. Engine is started and running for a calibrated amount of time. Remote start not active.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The park lock sensor detects a disengaged park lock for a calibrated amount of time when the desired position is PARK.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to power and ground circuits. Check Service Bulletins for possible causes that may apply. Remove the Transmission oil pan and inspect the park lock linkage and torsion spring for correct alignment or damage. Reinstall the Transmission oil pan. Connect the scan tool and clear the DTCs. If the DTC returns, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1daf-00 incompatible limp in action requested\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DAF-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCOMPATIBLE LIMP IN ACTION REQUESTED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to determine unique failure situations when multiple failures requiring conflicting limp-in actions occur. If conflicting limp-in actions are commanded, the mechanical limp-home mode is activated as the final limp-in action.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the ignition is on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Multiple failures requiring conflicting limp-in actions occur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via Controller Area Network (CAN). Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OTHER TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</li><li>ARE SET</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS ARE SET</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER TCM DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any other TCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair other TCM DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any PCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair PCM DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db0-00 implausible torque request signal sent\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB0-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE TORQUE REQUEST SIGNAL SENT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus, the transmitted messages on the CAN bus and the validity of the CAN signals. Several control units are connected to the CAN bus which send their messages cyclically in a defined time window. The messages contain multiple signals representing vehicle information</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN Signal Monitoring: If the sending control unit does not have valid information to send, it may send a</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">defined failure value indicating an invalid signal. Incoming signals with a defined failure value are monitored for signal validity. For some outgoing signals, the Transmission Control Module (TCM) reads its own signal back from the CAN to monitor the signal transmission for disturbances</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Ignition voltage within a calibrated range. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs). No CAN bus or message monitoring DTCs.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Transmission Control Module (TCM) detects implausible CAN torque request data from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Maximum system hydraulic pressure will be limited. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled. The TCM will not request any torque interventions from the PCM via CAN.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CAN BUS DTCS PRESENT</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS PRESENT</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) BUS DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any BCM CAN bus DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair BCM CAN bus DTCs. If DTC U0002 is set, perform that diagnostic first. Refer to</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0002-00 can c bus off performance .\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0002-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN C BUS OFF PERFORMANCE .</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any PCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE . Test complete.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db1-00 tcm system voltage excessively low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB1-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM SYSTEM VOLTAGE EXCESSIVELY LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors the system voltage level at the TCM supply voltage terminal for the following failure conditions:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">System Voltage Excessively Low System Voltage Low System Voltage High</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the TCM supply voltage is below a threshold that is lower than the System Voltage Excessively Low threshold, the TCM will not supply power to the solenoid valves and pressure regulators. A Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set when one of the diagnostic voltage thresholds is reached for a calibrated amount of time.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">High side switch is activated. When Shifter Position is in PARK or NEUTRAL: Engine speed via Controller Area Network (CAN) or input speed signal is above a calibrated value for a calibrated amount of time.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">When Shifter Position is in DRIVE or REVERSE: Engine speed via CAN or input speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The system voltage is less than a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OPEN FUSE</li><li>LOW BATTERY VOLTAGE</li><li>ENGINE CHARGING SYSTEM</li><li>BATTERY VOLTAGE CIRCUIT HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR ENGINE CHARGING SYSTEM DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Powertrain Control Module (PCM) DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any Engine Charging System DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair Charging System DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TCM SYSTEM VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, under Transmission, check system voltage.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Transmission system voltage above 9.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE TCM BATTERY CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the battery circuit at the TCM connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the battery circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db2-00 actuator supply voltage a circuit\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB2-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTUATOR SUPPLY VOLTAGE A CIRCUIT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The voltage supply circuit(s) for the solenoids and pressure regulators are monitored for open circuits, shorts to ground, and shorts to voltage. If a failure is detected, the Transmission Control Module (TCM) will deactivate the affected power supply circuit and set a corresponding Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) relevant to the fault that was detected.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Transmission Control Module (TCM) is in initialization.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The failure is detected if the activation of the output stage power supply has not succeeded.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to power and ground circuits. Check Service Bulletins for possible causes that may apply. Remove the Transmission oil pan and the TCM. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL . Inspect and clean the solenoid terminals at the wiring harness leadframe for metallic contamination. Reinstall the TCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), INSTALLATION . Connect the scan tool and erase the DTCs. Road test the vehicle and check for DTCs. If the DTC returns, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db3-00 tcm ecu reset recovery occurred\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB3-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM ECU RESET RECOVERY OCCURRED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to determine the reason of a reset after the reset occurred. Some of these are initiated by the Transmission Control Module (TCM) software and others may be caused by an under voltage condition. If the TCM detects a condition for initiating a reset, the reason of the reset is stored in an area of Random Access Memory (RAM) that is not initialized during TCM startup. Upon TCM startup this information is read out to store an appropriate Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicating the reason of the reset.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Reset monitoring is performed during initialization which occurs at power-up or after a reset.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The following failures can cause resets of the low level software: General exception (real time operating system, micro controller monitoring, division by zero, etc.). Watchdog communication failure. A safety function was not run in its defined cycle time. Monitoring of low level software safety functions indicates a failure. The following failures can cause resets of the high level software: Monitoring of Shift-By-Wire safety functions indicates a failure. Monitoring of Signal I/O safety functions indicates a failure. Failure to store safety relevant fault in the error handler (Error Reaction Manager). Failure to set safety relevant limp in action in the error handler (Error Reaction Manager). Monitoring of Shift-Control safety functions indicates a failure (electrical current not plausible, inconsistency of actual gear or target gear, power flow implausible, power flow inconsistent to actual gear, implausible combination of valves/clutches). If no information about the cause of the reset is stored, it is understood to be an under voltage condition. In this case, the active state (operation mode) of the operating system when the reset occurred is stored during: Initialization Normal operation mode Standby</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db4-00 incorrect gear ratio during gear engagement or in gear\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB4-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO DURING GEAR ENGAGEMENT OR IN GEAR</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fix gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db5-00 incorrect gear ratio during shift\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB5-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR RATIO DURING SHIFT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors for conditions which lead to an unexpected transmission gear ratio (e.g. slipping clutches, hydraulic or mechanical defects, etc.). The TCM compares the actual gear ratio (i.e. the ratio of input speed to output speed) to a minimum and maximum calibrated gear ratio value. The TCM performs this comparison while driving in a fix gear, during gear engagement, and during shifting from one gear to another.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shifter is in the Drive or Reverse position. Transmission oil temperature is above a calibrated value. No clutch slip control functions commanded. No Input Speed Sensor signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Input Speed Sensor signal is above a calibrated value. Output Speed Sensor signal is valid or the output speed can be calculated from the wheel speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal if the Output Speed Sensor signal is not available. Engine speed signal via CAN or output speed signal is above a calibrated value. During a gear shift: The output speed and the output speed gradient must be higher than a calibrated value. When a gear is engaged: The absolute value of the input speed gradient and pedal position must be lower than their respective calibrated values.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">After a calibrated number of failure symptoms are detected, a DTC is stored and the Transmission Control Module (TCM) commands a calibrated default gear. This gear is monitored as well and if a failure is detected for this gear, an alternative default gear is engaged and so on. The selection of alternative default gears follows a calibrated logic. This logic will detect a damaged clutch and to finally select an alternative gear that consists of a combination of clutches in which the damaged clutch is not involved. If a further failure symptom occurs in this final alternative default gear, a failure for general Transmission ratio malfunction is stored.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION - INTERNAL COMPONENTS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Remove the Transmission and perform the appropriate repair for this DTC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db6-00 vehicle speed signal performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB6-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">VEHICLE SPEED SIGNAL PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) can detect rationality failures of the input (turbine) speed sensor and output speed sensor signals as well as the wheel speed and engine speed signals received through the Controller Area Network (CAN).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The TCM performs three diagnostic checks that include:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Multi sensor comparisons of up to three speed signals (input, output and wheel speed). Monitoring of the gradient of the input speed signal. Double failure monitoring to determine unique failure situations which could require unique limp-in functionality.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No Input or Output Speed Sensor supply voltage Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. No Speed Sensor signal DTCs set. No Engine Speed or Wheel Speed Controller Area Network (CAN) signal DTCs set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The failure is detected if the difference between the wheel speed received via CAN and the following signals are both greater than a calibrated value for a calibrated amount of time: The calculated wheel speed from the output speed measured by the Transmission Control Module (TCM). The calculated wheel speed from the input speed measured by the TCM.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ANTI LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) DTCS ARE SET</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS ARE SET</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Diagnose Powertrain Control Module (PCM) and communication DTCs before proceeding. If no PCM or communication DTCs are set, diagnose Anti-Lock Brake System (ABS) DTCs before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FOR INTERNAL FAILURE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This DTC is an indication of a internal Transmission failure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the Transmission Oil Pan and inspect for excessive debris such as clutch friction material or metal contamination.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any indication of an internal Transmission failure?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair internal Transmission as necessary in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to DISASSEMBLY .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db7-00 torque converter clutch performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB7-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the monitoring is to detect a failure in the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) system. The TCC is used to bypass the torque converter. The TCC can be open, closed or in closed loop control mode where a specific clutch slip is controlled. The actual slip and the target slip are compared to detect a failure.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) closed or in closed loop control mode. Calculated pressure inside the TCC must be greater than a calibrated threshold. Engine torque must be lower than a calibrated threshold.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The difference between the actual slip and target slip of the TCC is greater than a calibrated threshold for an amount of time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will limit the current to the TCC solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TORQUE CONVERTER</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE . If the transmission does not pass the Verification Test, replace the Torque Converter in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to TORQUE CONVERTER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db8-00 unintended torque applied while in neutral\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB8-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">UNINTENDED TORQUE APPLIED WHILE IN NEUTRAL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to detect an unwanted power flow in the transmission. A rationality check of the ratio of input speed to engine speed is done while no power flow is requested.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No input speed signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No engine speed signal DTCs set. Engine speed is above a calibrated value. Mechanical Limp Home Mode is not active. No power flow requested.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ratio of input speed to engine speed is less than a calibrated value for a calibrated amount of time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. TCM will inhibit Transmission from being shifted out of PARK. Drive will be disabled. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL INCORRECT</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR INCORRECT GEAR RATIO (DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any Incorrect Gear Ratio DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair Incorrect Gear Ratio DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FLUID LEVEL</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the Transmission fluid level. Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Was the Transmission fluid level at the correct level?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Check transmission for leaks and repair in accordance with the Service Information. Fill Transmission to the proper fluid level. Refer to FLUID AND FILTER, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1db9-00 tcm ecu reset extended low voltage\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DB9-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM ECU RESET EXTENDED LOW VOLTAGE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to ensure power flow after a Transmission Control Module (TCM) reset during a mechanical limp-in action or after an under voltage reset due to a low voltage condition of the TCM source voltage.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Transmission Control Module (TCM) reset has occurred. Output speed is above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Reset has occurred with Mechanical Limp-In Action Active. Reset has occurred during an under voltage condition and the shifter position and driving direction information stored in Random Access Memory (RAM) has been cleared.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The TCM will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via Controller Area Network (CAN). Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS PRESENT</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR ENGINE CHARGING SYSTEM DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Powertrain Control Module (PCM) DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any Engine Charging System DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair Charging System DTCs before proceeding. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dc6-00 tcm not programmed\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DC6-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM NOT PROGRAMMED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) is programmed during manufacturing with generic software to facilitate testing. This software does not have the proper calibrations to control a transmission in a vehicle. The check for generic software is made at power-up. If generic software is detected by the controller the Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) will illuminate immediately and will stay illuminated until the proper software is installed.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will cause the Transmission to be placed into limp-in mode.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the ignition is on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Generic software is programmed in the Transmission Control Module (TCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) - PROGRAMMING ERROR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CONTROL MODULE PROGRAMMING ERROR</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set to inform the technician that the Transmission Control Module (TCM) is programmed with generic software and must be reprogrammed with vehicle specific software.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Perform the TCM PROGRAMMING PROCEDURE. Refer to MODULE PROGRAMMING .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Was the controller updated successfully?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dc7-00 clutch temp threshold achieved shift time reduction\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DC7-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CLUTCH TEMP THRESHOLD ACHIEVED SHIFT TIME REDUCTION</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) performs several diagnostic checks to determine whether the temperature of a clutch is above a calibrated temperature value. These diagnostic checks use temperature models which are based upon the following:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Input speed Output speed Current gear Target gear Calculated effective pressure on the engaging clutch Calculated effective pressure on the disengaging clutch</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set by these diagnostics are used to protect the durability of the clutches by controlling the shift operation. No repair action is required. This fault is only used to initiate a calibration strategy and for diagnostic information when other faults are set.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">A gear shift or gear engagement is active.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The calculated clutch temperature is above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Skip Shift function will be deactivated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>EXCESSIVE AMOUNT OF WIDE OPEN THROTTLE DRIVING</li><li>EXCESSIVE AMOUNT OF PADDLE SHIFT (IF EQUIPPED) USAGE IN LOW GEARS</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR OTHER TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           No repair action is required. This fault is only used to initiate a calibration strategy and for diagnostic information in case other faults are set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">View Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair other TCM DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dc8-00 clutch temp threshold achieved autostick inhibit\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DC8-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CLUTCH TEMP THRESHOLD ACHIEVED AUTOSTICK INHIBIT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) performs several diagnostic checks to determine whether the temperature of a clutch is above a calibrated temperature value. These diagnostic checks use temperature models which are based upon input speed and output speed, current gear, target gear, calculated effective pressure on engaging clutch and on the disengaging clutch. The Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set by these diagnostics are used to protect the durability of the clutches by controlling the shift operation. No repair action is required. This fault is only used to initiate a calibration strategy and for diagnostic information in case other faults are set.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">A gear shift or gear engagement is active.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The calculated clutch temperature is above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails. Auto Stick function will be deactivated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>EXCESSIVE AMOUNT OF WIDE OPEN THROTTLE DRIVING</li><li>EXCESSIVE AMOUNT OF PADDLE SHIFT USAGE IN LOW GEARS</li><li>Always perform the DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to</li><li>PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR OTHER TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           No repair action is required if no other DTCs are set. This fault is usually set from excessive paddle shifter use.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">View Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair other TCM DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dc9-00 clutch temp threshold achieved skip shift down inhibit\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DC9-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CLUTCH TEMP THRESHOLD ACHIEVED SKIP SHIFT DOWN INHIBIT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) performs several diagnostic checks to determine whether the temperature of a clutch is above a calibrated temperature value. These diagnostic checks use temperature models which are based upon input speed and output speed, current gear, target gear, calculated effective pressure on engaging clutch and on the disengaging clutch. The Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set by these diagnostics are used to protect the durability of the clutches by controlling the shift operation. No repair action is required. This fault is only used to initiate a calibration strategy and for diagnostic information in case other faults are set.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">A gear shift or gear engagement is active.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The calculated clutch temperature is above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Maximum Torque Reduction function will be activated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>EXCESSIVE AMOUNT OF WIDE OPEN THROTTLE DRIVING</li><li>EXCESSIVE AMOUNT OF PADDLE SHIFT USAGE IN LOW GEARS (IF EQUIPPED)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR OTHER TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           No repair action is required. This fault is only used to initiate a calibration strategy and for diagnostic information in case other faults are set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">View Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair other TCM DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dca-00 park sense circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DCA-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PARK SENSE CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor the park sense circuit from the Radio Frequency (RF) Hub. The RF Hub supplies B (+) on the park circuit to the Transmission Control Module (TCM). When the transmission is in park, the TCM will ground the park circuit indicating to the RF Hub that the transmission is in park. If the TCM detects an open or short to ground on the park circuit, a Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will set.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Open or short to ground on the park circuit between the Transmission Control Module (TCM) and the Radio Frequency (RF) Hub.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PARK CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>PARK CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RADIO FREQUENCY (RF) HUB</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the Shifter and the Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) is correctly displaying PARK (not flashing), this indicates the Transmission Control Module (TCM) is sending a Controller Area Network (CAN) message that the Transmission is in the park position.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (T824) PARK CIRCUIT VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Transmission Assembly harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect the Engine harness side of the Transmission Assembly harness connector for bent or backed out terminals, corrosion, and other terminal damage. Repair as necessary.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (T824) Park circuit at the Transmission Assembly harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage above 10.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Check the terminals in the Transmission Assembly harness connector for damaged or loose terminals, or terminals that are backed out of the connector. Reconnect the Transmission Assembly harness connector and erase DTCs.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (T824) PARK CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Radio Frequency (RF) Hub C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (T824) Park circuit between the Transmission Assembly harness connector and the RF Hub C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (T824) Park circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK (T824) PARK CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (T824) Park circuit at the Transmission Assembly harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (T824) Park circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (T824) Park circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the RF Hub connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to power and ground circuits. Check Service Bulletins for possible causes that may apply. If no problems are found, replace and program the RF Hub in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, RADIO FREQUENCY (RF HUB), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE . Test Complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dcd-00 tcm monitoring processor performance multiple clutches locked\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DCD-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM MONITORING PROCESSOR PERFORMANCE MULTIPLE CLUTCHES LOCKED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">UP</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors the pressure regulator and solenoid logic to detect a failure in the activation of the pressure regulators and solenoids. The pressure regulators are used to control the pressure to the clutches and the solenoids are used to activate the pressure to the parking lock and to the position</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">valve. The commanded currents of all regulators and solenoids are monitored. The monitoring consists of several diagnostic strategies:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Transmission blocking (Multiple clutches locked up) Wrong driving direction (Incorrect driving direction) Gear engagement of Reverse gear while driving forward (Unallowed Reverse engagement) Unwanted engaging or disengaging of Parking Lock (Unallowed Park engagement)</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Limp home mode is not active. Position valve monitoring not active. Transmission oil temperature must be above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">More than three pressure regulators are activated at the same time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CLUTCH A</li><li>CLUTCH B</li><li>CLUTCH C</li><li>CLUTCH D</li><li>CLUTCH E</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dce-00 tcm monitoring processor performance incorrect driving\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DCE-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM MONITORING PROCESSOR PERFORMANCE INCORRECT DRIVING</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DIRECTION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors the pressure regulator and solenoid logic to detect a failure in the activation of the pressure regulators and solenoids. The pressure regulators are used to control the pressure to the clutches and the solenoids are used to activate the pressure to the parking lock and to the position valve. The commanded currents of all regulators and solenoids are monitored. The monitoring consists of several diagnostic strategies:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Transmission blocking (Multiple clutches locked up) Wrong driving direction (Incorrect driving direction) Gear engagement of Reverse gear while driving forward (Unallowed Reverse engagement) Unwanted engaging or disengaging of Parking Lock (Unallowed Park engagement)</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Limp home mode is not active. Position valve monitoring not active. Shifter is in DRIVE or REVERSE position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When Shifter is in DRIVE: A pressure regulator combination for reverse gear is detected (clutches A, B and D activated). When Shifter is in REVERSE: A pressure regulator combination different from reverse gear is detected (clutch C or E activated).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CLUTCH A</li><li>CLUTCH B</li><li>CLUTCH C</li><li>CLUTCH D</li><li>CLUTCH E</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dcf-00 tcm monitoring processor performance unallowed park\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DCF-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM MONITORING PROCESSOR PERFORMANCE UNALLOWED PARK</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ENGAGEMENT DUE TO ABS FAILURE</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors the pressure regulator and solenoid logic to detect a failure in the activation of the pressure regulators and solenoids. The pressure regulators are used to control the pressure to the clutches and the solenoids are used to activate the pressure to the parking lock and to the position valve. The commanded currents of all regulators and solenoids are monitored. The monitoring consists of several diagnostic strategies:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Transmission blocking (Multiple clutches locked up) Wrong driving direction (Incorrect driving direction) Gear engagement of Reverse gear while driving forward (Unallowed Reverse engagement) Unwanted engaging or disengaging of Parking Lock (Unallowed Park engagement)</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Limp home mode is not active. Position valve monitoring is not active. Vehicle speed signal is not valid.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The solenoid valve for the park lock is deactivated for greater than a calibrated amount of time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ABS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ABS DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair ABS DTCS. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dd0-00 tcm monitoring processor performance unallowed park\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DD0-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM MONITORING PROCESSOR PERFORMANCE UNALLOWED PARK</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ENGAGEMENT</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors the pressure regulator and solenoid logic to detect a failure in the activation of the pressure regulators and solenoids. The pressure regulators are used to control the pressure to the clutches and the solenoids are used to activate the pressure to the parking lock and to the position valve. The commanded currents of all regulators and solenoids are monitored. The monitoring consists of several diagnostic strategies:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Transmission blocking (Multiple clutches locked up) Wrong driving direction (Incorrect driving direction) Gear engagement of Reverse gear while driving forward (Unallowed Reverse engagement) Unwanted engaging or disengaging of Parking Lock (Unallowed Park engagement)</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Limp home mode is not active. Position valve monitoring is not active. Shifter is in PARK position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The solenoid for the position valve or the pressure regulator of clutch C is activated for a calibrated amount of time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dd1-00 input turbine speed sensor 1 gradient fault\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DD1-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INPUT TURBINE SPEED SENSOR 1 GRADIENT FAULT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) can detect rationality failures of the input (turbine) speed sensor and output speed sensor signals as well as the wheel speed and engine speed signals received through the Controller Area Network (CAN).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The TCM performs three diagnostic checks that include:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Multi sensor comparisons of up to three speed signals (input, output and wheel speed). Monitoring of the gradient of the input speed signal. Double failure monitoring to determine unique failure situations which could require unique limp-in functionality.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No sensor supply voltage Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. No electrical DTCs set for sensors used in this diagnostic. No Controller Area Network (CAN) DTCs set for speed signals used in the diagnostic.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The input speed gradient is less than a calibrated value for a calibrated amount of time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via CAN. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Maximum system hydraulic pressure will be limited. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>P4 ANNULUS DRUM</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Raise the vehicle on the hoist.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor the Input Speed Sensor rpm.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Firmly apply the brake pedal and place the gear selector in Drive.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        To avoid personal injury or death, keep hands and feet clear of rotating wheels.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Release the brakes and raise the engine speed to allow the Transmission to perform a 2-3 and 3-4 upshift.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the Input Speed Sensor display an rpm above 7, 700?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK TRANSMISSION FOR INTERNAL FAILURE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC is an indication of a internal Transmission failure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the Transmission Oil Pan and inspect for excessive debris such as clutch friction material or metal contamination.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any indication of an internal Transmission failure?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair internal Transmission as necessary in accordance with the Service Information. Verify the surface of the P4 annulus drum is not damaged. Refer to DISASSEMBLY .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dd2-00 torque request signal from tcm denied\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DD2-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TORQUE REQUEST SIGNAL FROM TCM DENIED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus, the transmitted messages on the CAN bus, and the validity of the CAN signals. Several control units are connected to the CAN bus which send their messages cyclically in a defined time window. The messages contain multiple signals representing vehicle information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN Signal Monitoring: If the sending control unit does not have valid information to send, it may send a</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">defined failure value indicating an invalid signal. Incoming signals with a defined failure value are monitored for signal validity. For some outgoing signals, the Transmission Control Module (TCM) reads its own signal back from the CAN bus to monitor the signal transmission for disturbances.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage within a calibrated range. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. No CAN bus message monitoring DTCs set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A fault is detected if any of the following conditions occur: The incoming signal is set to a default value indicating an invalid signal. The incoming signal has a validity bit set in the message indicating an invalid signal. The value of the outgoing signal is not equal to the feedback signal which is immediately read back by the TCM.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via CAN. The TCM will limit the current to the Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) solenoid to 50mA. The TCC will be open. Maximum system hydraulic pressure will be limited. Shift adaptation functions will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CAN BUS DTCS SET</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS SET</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS SET</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any BCM CAN bus DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair BCM CAN bus DTCs in accordance with the Service Information. If DTC U0002 is set, perform that diagnostic first. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any PCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair PCM DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any other TCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair other TCM DTC(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1ddc-00 tcm monitoring processor performance unallowed reverse\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DDC-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM MONITORING PROCESSOR PERFORMANCE UNALLOWED REVERSE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ENGAGEMENT</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors the pressure regulator and solenoid logic to detect a failure in the activation of the pressure regulators and solenoids. The pressure regulators are used to control the pressure to the clutches and the solenoids are used to activate the pressure to the parking lock and to the position valve. The commanded currents of all regulators and solenoids are monitored. The monitoring consists of several diagnostic strategies:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Transmission blocking (Multiple clutches locked up) Wrong driving direction (Incorrect driving direction) Gear engagement of Reverse gear while driving forward (Unallowed Reverse engagement) Unwanted engaging or disengaging of Parking Lock (Unallowed Park engagement)</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Limp home mode is not active. Position valve monitoring is not active. No vehicle speed signal Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Vehicle speed above calibrated value. Power flow is in a forward direction.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A failure is detected if a pressure regulator combination for reverse gear is detected (clutches A, B and D activated).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1ddd-00 tcm monitoring performance unable to disengage drive or\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DDD-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM MONITORING PERFORMANCE UNABLE TO DISENGAGE DRIVE OR</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">REVERSE</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to detect a failure in the activation of the pressure regulators during gear</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">disengagement or while NEUTRAL or PARK position is engaged. This is a rationality check between the activated pressure regulators and the shifter selected gear.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Gear Disengagement: Shifter is in PARK or NEUTRAL. Three pressure regulators are activated. Neutral or Park: Shifter is in PARK or NEUTRAL. Since the requested position change to PARK or NEUTRAL, the number of activated pressure regulators has been less than three for more than a calibrated amount of time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Gear Disengagement: A failure is detected during gear disengagement if three or more pressure regulators are activated at the same time for a calibrated amount of time. Neutral or Park: A failure is detected while in Neutral or Park position is engaged if in addition to the two pressure regulators a third pressure regulator is activated at the same time for a calibrated amount of time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dde-00 ignition run-start input 1-2 correlation\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DDE-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IGNITION RUN-START INPUT 1-2 CORRELATION</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor if the hard-wired ignition signal state is equal to the ignition signal state received on the Controller Area Network (CAN) BUS. The CAN message is sent by the Body Control Module (BCM) to the Transmission Control Module (TCM).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">A low battery State Of Charge (SOC) or a charging system that is not operating properly can cause many symptoms and DTCs to set. If possibly related to the customer complaint, check the vehicle charging system and battery for proper operation . Refer to the appropriate Service Information.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. No Controller Area Network (CAN) BUS monitoring or CAN message monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The hard wired ignition signal to the Transmission Control Module (TCM) is not equal to the ignition</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">signal that is transmitted on the CAN bus from the Body Control Module (BCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) BUS DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any TCM CAN bus DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair TCM CAN bus DTCs. If DTC U0001-CAN C BUS is set, perform that diagnostic first. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any PCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1deb-00 incorrect gear displayed due to incorrect gear ratio\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DEB-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INCORRECT GEAR DISPLAYED DUE TO INCORRECT GEAR RATIO</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to ensure that N is displayed to the driver when a ratio monitoring failure requires a limp-in action in neutral position.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Engine speed above a calibrated value. Shifter request is REVERSE or DRIVE. A ratio monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set which initiates a limp-in action in Neutral position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The displayed position to the driver is R or D.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE ASSEMBLY (TCMA)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR INCORRECT GEAR RATIO DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any Incorrect Gear Ratio DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair Incorrect Gear Ratio DTCs before proceeding. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1df3-00 ecu not initialized\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DF3-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU NOT INITIALIZED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor the time period of the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) initialization state. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) receives the status of the initialization state from the ESM on the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus while evaluating a counter in the TCM to determine if the initialization</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">time is excessive.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. No Controller Area Network (CAN) monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Battery voltage is above a calibrated value. No shifter reset requested.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The time period of the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) initialization is greater than a calibrated amount of time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. Transmission Control Module (TCM) will inhibit Transmission from being shifted out of PARK. Reverse will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) BUS DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any TCM CAN bus DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair TCM CAN bus DTCs. If DTC U0001-CAN C BUS is set, perform that diagnostic first. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK IF ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) DTCS ARE PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are any ESM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair ESM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1df7-00 actual decrease of engine torque low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DF7-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTUAL DECREASE OF ENGINE TORQUE LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor if the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) executed the torque requested by the Transmission Control Module (TCM). This is determined by comparing the PCM&#x27;s executed torque to the original torque requested by the TCM over the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus. These torque requests only occur during shift operations. This diagnostic checks for engine torque reduction too low.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. No CAN bus message monitoring DTCs set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Executed engine torque reduction is lower than the requested engine torque reduction by a calibrated amount.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) BUS DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any TCM CAN bus DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair TCM CAN bus DTCs. If DTC U0001-CAN C BUS is set, perform that diagnostic first. DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any PCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1df8-00 actual decrease of engine torque high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DF8-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTUAL DECREASE OF ENGINE TORQUE HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor if the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) executed the torque requested by the Transmission Control Module (TCM). This is determined by comparing the PCM&#x27;s executed</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">torque to the original torque requested by the TCM over the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus. These torque requests only occur during shift operations. This diagnostic checks for engine torque reduction too high.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTCs) set. No CAN message monitoring DTCS set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Executed engine torque reduction is higher than the requested engine torque reduction by a calibrated amount.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) BUS DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any TCM CAN bus DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair TCM CAN bus DTCs. If DTC U0001-CAN C BUS is set, perform that diagnostic first. DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any PCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1df9-00 actual increase of engine torque low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DF9-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTUAL INCREASE OF ENGINE TORQUE LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor if the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) executed the torque requested by the Transmission Control Module (TCM). This is determined by comparing the PCM&#x27;s executed torque to the original torque requested by the TCM over the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus. These torque requests only occur during shift operations. This diagnostic checks for engine torque increase too low.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. No CAN message monitoring DTCs set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Executed engine torque increase is lower than the requested engine torque increase by a calibrated amount.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR TCM CAN BUS DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any TCM CAN bus DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair TCM CAN bus DTCs in accordance with the Service Information. If DTC U0001- CAN C BUS is set, perform that diagnostic first. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK IF PCM DTCS ARE PRESENT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any PCM DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair PCM DTCs in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) terminals</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">for corrosion, damage, and pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1dfa-00 actual increase of engine torque high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1DFA-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTUAL INCREASE OF ENGINE TORQUE HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor if the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) executed the torque requested by the Transmission Control Module (TCM). This is determined by comparing the PCM&#x27;s executed torque to the original torque requested by the TCM over the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus. These torque requests only occur during shift operations. This diagnostic checks for engine torque increase too high.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No CAN message monitoring DTCs set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Executed engine torque increase is higher than the requested engine torque increase by a calibrated amount.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) BUS DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any TCM CAN bus DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair TCM CAN bus DTCs. If DTC U0001-CAN C BUS is set, perform that diagnostic first. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any PCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p215c-00 output shaft speed wheel speed correlation\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P215C-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">OUTPUT SHAFT SPEED WHEEL SPEED CORRELATION</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Vehicle Speed Sensor (VSS) signal is transmitted to the Anti-Lock Brake System (ABS) Module via dedicated hard wire. The VSS signal is then transmitted over the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus to the Transmission Control Module (TCM).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Output Speed Sensor signal is a direct input to the TCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The TCM monitors these signals to determine if the VSS signal CAN message is valid. If the VSS signal and the Output Speed Sensor signal do not match, this Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect tire size may influence this DTC. If the incorrect tire size is programmed into the BCM, this can contribute to this DTC.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          A non-production size tire cannot be programmed into the BCM. The production Powertrain, with the production size tires, is the only emissions certified configuration that is available for reprogramming.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. The shifter is in a forward gear. No Antilock Brake System (ABS) or Output Speed Sensor DTCs set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Vehicle Speed Sensor signal received via CAN and the Output Speed Sensor signal values do not match.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission Control Module will not request any positive torque interventions from the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via CAN.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LOSS OF COMMUNICATION WITH THE ANTI LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ANTILOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ABS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is DTC U0121-Lost Communication With ABS Module set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair DTC U0121-Lost Communication With ABS Module. Refer to U0121-00-LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL MODULE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p2761-00 torque converter clutch pressure control solenoid control\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P2761-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PRESSURE CONTROL SOLENOID CONTROL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CIRCUIT-OPEN</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The diagnostics are able to detect circuit failures on any of the output stages in the Transmission Control Module (TCM). All output stages are controlled by a current controller that can operate an output stage in two different modes:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Current controlled mode (pressure regulators) Switched mode or Pulse Width Modulated (PWM) controlled (solenoids)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pressure Regulator Monitoring: The current regulator in the TCM indicates the following circuit failures to the Central Processing Unit (CPU):</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Short to battery Bypass to ground (high resistance short to ground) Short to ground or open circuit (can only be distinguished when the output stage is in idle mode, i.e. commanded current is 0 mA)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In addition to the circuit failure information, the TCM monitoring software uses a PWM feedback signal generated by the current regulator in the output stage to identify failures. To perform rationality monitoring of the output stage current, the TCM software calculates the actual current dependent on the PWM feedback signal, the output stage power supply voltage and the actual transmission oil temperature. The TCM can only</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">distinguish between a short to ground and an open circuit failure if the output stage is deactivated. Depending on the required time to bring the transmission into a limp home mode, a further evaluation of the failure is determined after switching off the output stage in order to distinguish between both failure types.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Solenoid Monitoring: The TCM measures the actual solenoid voltages and compares them to calibrated values to identify the following electrical failures:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Short to battery Open circuit Short to ground</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the solenoid is switched on (i.e. commanded control value is 100%), the diagnostic can not distinguish between short to ground and open circuit. In that case, the Application-Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) status information is used to detect the failure.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Pressure Control Solenoids: Ignition on. Output stages power supply is activated. Shift Solenoids: Short to Battery: Output stages power supply is activated. Output stage is commanded above 5% Pulse Width Modulated (PWM). Open Circuit or Short to Ground: Output stages power supply is activated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pressure Control Solenoids: A short to battery failure is detected if the Application-Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) indicates a short to battery failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 0%. An open circuit or short to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to ground or open circuit failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 100%. A short to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to ground failure in reaction to the output stage being switch off after an open circuit or short to ground failure detection. A bypass to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a bypass to ground failure. A current too low failure is detected if the calculated pressure control solenoid current is less than a calibrated value. A current too high failure is detected if the calculated pressure control solenoid current is greater than a calibrated value. A Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI) communication failure in the SPI communication between the Central Processing Unit (CPU) and the ASIC is detected based upon the validity of the check-byte, the timing and the feedback signal of the message. Shift Solenoids:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">A short to battery failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty phase is greater than a calibrated value. An open circuit failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty or no duty phase is in an invalid range. A short to ground failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty or no duty phase is less than a calibrated value. A short to ground or open circuit failure is detected if the commanded duty cycle for the solenoid is 100% and the ASIC indicates the output stage is switched off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails. Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) Solenoid will be commanded off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PRESSURE CONTROL SOLENOID</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE ASSEMBLY (TCMA)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to power and ground circuits. Check Service Bulletins for possible causes that may apply. Remove the Transmission oil pan and the TCM. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL . Inspect and clean the solenoid terminals at the wiring harness leadframe for metallic contamination. Reinstall the TCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), INSTALLATION . Connect the scan tool and erase the DTCs. Road test the vehicle and check for DTCs. If the DTC returns, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p2762-00 torque converter clutch pressure control solenoid control\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P2762-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PRESSURE CONTROL SOLENOID CONTROL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CIRCUIT RANGE PERFORMANCE</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The diagnostics are able to detect circuit failures on any of the output stages in the Transmission Control Module (TCM). All output stages are controlled by a current controller that can operate an output stage in two different modes:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Current controlled mode (pressure regulators) Switched mode or Pulse Width Modulated (PWM) controlled (solenoids)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pressure Regulator Monitoring: The current regulator in the TCM indicates the following circuit failures to the Central Processing Unit (CPU):</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Short to battery Bypass to ground (high resistance short to ground) Short to ground or open circuit (can only be distinguished when the output stage is in idle mode, i.e. commanded current is 0 mA)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In addition to the circuit failure information, the TCM monitoring software uses a PWM feedback signal generated by the current regulator in the output stage to identify failures. To perform rationality monitoring of the output stage current, the TCM software calculates the actual current dependent on the PWM feedback signal, the output stage power supply voltage and the actual transmission oil temperature. The TCM can only</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">distinguish between a short to ground and an open circuit failure if the output stage is deactivated. Depending on the required time to bring the transmission into a limp home mode, a further evaluation of the failure is determined after switching off the output stage in order to distinguish between both failure types.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Solenoid Monitoring: The TCM measures the actual solenoid voltages and compares them to calibrated values to identify the following electrical failures:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Short to battery Open circuit Short to ground</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the solenoid is switched on (i.e. commanded control value is 100%), the diagnostic can not distinguish between short to ground and open circuit. In that case, the Application-Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) status information is used to detect the failure.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Pressure Control Solenoids: Ignition on. Output stages power supply is activated. Shift Solenoids: Short to Battery: Output stages power supply is activated. Output stage is commanded above 5% Pulse Width Modulated (PWM). Open Circuit or Short to Ground: Output stages power supply is activated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pressure Control Solenoids: A short to battery failure is detected if the Application-Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) indicates a short to battery failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 0%. An open circuit or short to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to ground or open circuit failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 100%. A short to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to ground failure in reaction to the output stage being switch off after an open circuit or short to ground failure detection. A bypass to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a bypass to ground failure. A current too low failure is detected if the calculated pressure control solenoid current is less than a calibrated value. A current too high failure is detected if the calculated pressure control solenoid current is greater than a calibrated value. A Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI) communication failure in the SPI communication between the Central Processing Unit (CPU) and the ASIC is detected based upon the validity of the check-byte, the timing and the feedback signal of the message. Shift Solenoids:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">A short to battery failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty phase is greater than a calibrated value. An open circuit failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty or no duty phase is in an invalid range. A short to ground failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty or no duty phase is less than a calibrated value. A short to ground or open circuit failure is detected if the commanded duty cycle for the solenoid is 100% and the ASIC indicates the output stage is switched off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PRESSURE CONTROL SOLENOID</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE ASSEMBLY (TCMA)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to power and ground circuits. Check Service Bulletins for possible causes that may apply. Remove the Transmission oil pan and the TCM. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL . Inspect and clean the solenoid terminals at the wiring harness leadframe for metallic contamination. Reinstall the TCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), INSTALLATION . Connect the scan tool and erase the DTCs. Road test the vehicle and check for DTCs. If the DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">returns, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p2763-00 torque converter clutch pressure control solenoid control\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P2763-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PRESSURE CONTROL SOLENOID CONTROL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CIRCUIT HIGH</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The diagnostics are able to detect circuit failures on any of the output stages in the Transmission Control Module (TCM). All output stages are controlled by a current controller that can operate an output stage in two different modes:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Current controlled mode (pressure regulators) Switched mode or Pulse Width Modulated (PWM) controlled (solenoids)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pressure Regulator Monitoring: The current regulator in the TCM indicates the following circuit failures to the Central Processing Unit (CPU):</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Short to battery Bypass to ground (high resistance short to ground) Short to ground or open circuit (can only be distinguished when the output stage is in idle mode, i.e. commanded current is 0 mA)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In addition to the circuit failure information, the TCM monitoring software uses a PWM feedback signal generated by the current regulator in the output stage to identify failures. To perform rationality monitoring of the output stage current, the TCM software calculates the actual current dependent on the PWM feedback signal, the output stage power supply voltage and the actual transmission oil temperature. The TCM can only</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">distinguish between a short to ground and an open circuit failure if the output stage is deactivated. Depending on the required time to bring the transmission into a limp home mode, a further evaluation of the failure is determined after switching off the output stage in order to distinguish between both failure types.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Solenoid Monitoring: The TCM measures the actual solenoid voltages and compares them to calibrated values to identify the following electrical failures:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Short to battery Open circuit Short to ground</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the solenoid is switched on (i.e. commanded control value is 100%), the diagnostic can not distinguish between short to ground and open circuit. In that case, the Application-Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) status information is used to detect the failure.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Pressure Control Solenoids: Ignition on. Output stages power supply is activated. Shift Solenoids: Short to Battery: Output stages power supply is activated. Output stage is commanded above 5% Pulse Width Modulated (PWM). Open Circuit or Short to Ground: Output stages power supply is activated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pressure Control Solenoids: A short to battery failure is detected if the Application-Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) indicates a short to battery failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 0%. A short to battery failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to battery failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 0%. An open circuit or short to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to ground or open circuit failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 100%. A short to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to ground failure in reaction to the output stage being switch off after an open circuit or short to ground failure detection. A bypass to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a bypass to ground failure. A current too low failure is detected if the calculated pressure control solenoid current is less than a calibrated value. A current too high failure is detected if the calculated pressure control solenoid current is greater than a calibrated value. A Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI) communication failure in the SPI communication between the Central Processing Unit (CPU) and the ASIC is detected based upon the validity of the check-byte,</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">the timing and the feedback signal of the message. Shift Solenoids: A short to battery failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty phase is greater than a calibrated value. An open circuit failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty or no duty phase is in an invalid range. A short to ground failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty or no duty phase is less than a calibrated value. A short to ground or open circuit failure is detected if the commanded duty cycle for the solenoid is 100% and the ASIC indicates the output stage is switched off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated. Torque Converter Clutch (TCC) Low Side Pressure Regulator Switch will be commanded off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PRESSURE CONTROL SOLENOID</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE ASSEMBLY (TCMA)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to power and ground circuits. Check Service Bulletins for possible causes that may apply. Remove the Transmission oil pan and the TCM. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL . Inspect and clean the solenoid terminals at the wiring harness leadframe for metallic contamination. Reinstall the TCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), INSTALLATION . Connect the scan tool and erase the DTCs. Road test the vehicle and check for DTCs. If the DTC returns, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p2764-00 torque converter clutch pressure control solenoid control\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P2764-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PRESSURE CONTROL SOLENOID CONTROL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CIRCUIT LOW</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The diagnostics are able to detect circuit failures on any of the output stages in the Transmission Control Module (TCM). All output stages are controlled by a current controller that can operate an output stage in two different modes:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Current controlled mode (pressure regulators) Switched mode or Pulse Width Modulated (PWM) controlled (solenoids)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pressure Regulator Monitoring: The current regulator in the TCM indicates the following circuit failures to the Central Processing Unit (CPU):</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Short to battery Bypass to ground (high resistance short to ground) Short to ground or open circuit (can only be distinguished when the output stage is in idle mode, i.e. commanded current is 0 mA)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In addition to the circuit failure information, the TCM monitoring software uses a PWM feedback signal generated by the current regulator in the output stage to identify failures. To perform rationality monitoring of the output stage current, the TCM software calculates the actual current dependent on the PWM feedback signal, the output stage power supply voltage and the actual transmission oil temperature. The TCM can only</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">distinguish between a short to ground and an open circuit failure if the output stage is deactivated. Depending on the required time to bring the transmission into a limp home mode, a further evaluation of the failure is determined after switching off the output stage in order to distinguish between both failure types.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Solenoid Monitoring: The TCM measures the actual solenoid voltages and compares them to calibrated values to identify the following electrical failures:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Short to battery Open circuit Short to ground</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the solenoid is switched on (i.e. commanded control value is 100%), the diagnostic can not distinguish between short to ground and open circuit. In that case, the Application-Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) status information is used to detect the failure.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Pressure Control Solenoids: Ignition on. Output stages power supply is activated. Shift Solenoids: Short to Battery: Output stages power supply is activated. Output stage is commanded above 5% Pulse Width Modulated (PWM). Open Circuit or Short to Ground: Output stages power supply is activated.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pressure Control Solenoids: A short to battery failure is detected if the Application-Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) indicates a short to battery failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 0%. A short to battery failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to battery failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 0%. An open circuit or short to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to ground or open circuit failure or the PWM feedback signal at the output stage is 100%. A short to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a short to ground failure in reaction to the output stage being switch off after an open circuit or short to ground failure detection. A bypass to ground failure is detected if the ASIC indicates a bypass to ground failure. A current too low failure is detected if the calculated pressure control solenoid current is less than a calibrated value. A current too high failure is detected if the calculated pressure control solenoid current is greater than a calibrated value. A Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI) communication failure in the SPI communication between the Central Processing Unit (CPU) and the ASIC is detected based upon the validity of the check-byte,</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">the timing and the feedback signal of the message. Shift Solenoids: A short to battery failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty phase is greater than a calibrated value. An open circuit failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty or no duty phase is in an invalid range. A short to ground failure is detected if the voltage of the output signal during PWM duty or no duty phase is less than a calibrated value. A short to ground or open circuit failure is detected if the commanded duty cycle for the solenoid is 100% and the ASIC indicates the output stage is switched off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Malfunction Indicator Lamp (MIL) is illuminated on the first trip that the diagnostic fails. The Transmission will be placed into Limp-in mode. Remote Start feature, if equipped, will be disabled. Special shifting modes (Sport Mode, Winter Mode, Manual Mode, etc.,) will be disabled. Start/Stop feature, if equipped, will be disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TORQUE CONVERTER CLUTCH PRESSURE CONTROL SOLENOID</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE ASSEMBLY (TCMA)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to power and ground circuits. Check Service Bulletins for possible causes that may apply. Remove the Transmission oil pan and the TCM. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL . Inspect and clean the solenoid</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">terminals at the wiring harness leadframe for metallic contamination. Reinstall the TCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), INSTALLATION . Connect the scan tool and erase the DTCs. Road test the vehicle and check for DTCs. If the DTC returns, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0001-00 can c bus\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0001-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN C BUS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an in-depth explanation of the CAN Bus network operation, refer to DESCRIPTION .</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition is on. Battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN C bus has experienced a failure due to a circuit or processor fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OPEN OR SHORTED CAN C BUS CIRCUIT</li><li>CAN C RELATED MODULE</li><li>CAN C RELATED STAR CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li><li>CAN C RELATED SPLICE BLOCK CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>ATTEMPT TO DUPLICATE THE CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         This DTC sets when the CAN C bus is disabled. If the scan tool is able to read this DTC, then the fault is currently NOT active. This diagnostic procedure only troubleshoots an intermittent condition. Follow this procedure to attempt to locate the intermittent condition or induce the fault so the diagnostic procedures under SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C in Section 29 can be followed.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, run a Vehicle Scan Report and attached it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the fault now present?</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the fault is present, the scan tool will not communicate with modules on the CAN C bus.</div><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ATTEMPT TO LOCATE AN INTERMITTENT CIRCUIT FAULT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The scan tool LOSS OF COMM TEST will force the modules on the CAN C bus to continuously ping each other.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, initiate the LOSS OF COMM TEST.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          A value above 0 under the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES can help indicate the location of a circuit fault while wiggling the related CAN C bus circuits.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The scan tool lag time between pings is almost 1 full second. Keep this in mind while wiggling the wires and connectors.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>In a systematic manner, wiggle the applicable CAN C circuits at each related module, in-line connector, and Star/Splice Block Connector (if equipped) while monitoring the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES on the scan tool.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the above test help locate the fault?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform repairs as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>PERFORM VISUAL INSPECTION OF CONNECTORS, TERMINALS AND WIRES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all CAN C related modules harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Reconnect all CAN C related modules harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, attempt to communicate with the CAN C bus.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool communicate with the CAN C bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this DTC to set are no longer present. Test complete.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0074-00 dedicated powertrain (dpt) can bus off\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0074-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DEDICATED POWERTRAIN (DPT) CAN BUS OFF</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus, the transmitted messages on the CAN bus and the validity of the CAN signals. Several control units are connected to the CAN bus which send their messages cyclically in a defined time window. The messages contain multiple signals representing vehicle information.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage within a valid range. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. No CAN bus or message monitoring DTCs set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) detects an open, short to ground, or short to voltage on the CAN C bus circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN C BUS CIRCUITS OPEN OR SHORTED</li><li>DTCS RELATED TO BATTERY VOLTAGE, IGNITION OR VIN MESSAGES</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) POWER AND GROUND</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>MODULE THAT SET THIS DTC</li><li>Always perform the DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to</li><li>PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           For vehicle communication problems, use the scan tool to refer to the Network Review Screen. The screen depicts a high level view of the vehicle network. Fault and problem areas appear in red. Selecting any of the network components allows access to the source of the problem.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is this DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform U0002-Controller Area Network (CAN) C BUS Off Performance diagnostic procedure.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to U0002-00-CAN C BUS OFF PERFORMANCE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the Stored Lost Communication DTCs diagnostic procedure. Refer to STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0100-00 lost communication with ecm/pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0100-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ECM/PCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ECM/PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0103-00 lost communication with electric gear shift module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0103-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ELECTRIC GEAR SHIFT MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ELECTRIC GEAR SHIFT MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0121-00 lost communication with anti-lock brake system (abs) control\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0121-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MODULE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0128-00 lost communication with park brake control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0128-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH PARK BRAKE CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع PARK BRAKE CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0140-00 lost communication with body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0140-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0155-00 lost communication with cluster-ccn\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0155-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH CLUSTER-CCN</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع CLUSTER-CCN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0212-00 lost communication with scm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0212-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH SCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع SCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0401-00 implausible data received from ecm/pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0401-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ECM/PCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ECM/PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0404-00 implausible data received from esm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0404-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ESM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ESM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0415-00 implausible data received from abs\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0415-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ABS</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ABS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0422-00 implausible data received from body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0422-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0423-00 implausible data received from cluster-ccn\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0423-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM CLUSTER-CCN</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من CLUSTER-CCN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0429-00 implausible data received from scm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0429-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM SCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من SCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u11e3-00 tcm lost communication with esm on dpt can\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U11E3-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ESM ON DPT CAN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus, the transmitted messages on the CAN bus and the validity of the CAN signals. Several control units are connected to the CAN bus which send their messages cyclically in a defined time window. The messages contain multiple signals representing vehicle information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN Bus Monitoring: To distinguish general problems with the CAN bus (e.g. electrical problems) from problems with certain messages or signals, the general state of the CAN bus is monitored.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN Message Monitoring: All messages received and used by the Transmission Control Module (TCM) are monitored for timeout and validity of the Data Length Code (DLC) information in the message header. If</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">available, the message is also monitored for the validity of a checksum and for the correct behavior of an alive- counter that the sending control unit is expected to increment on each transmittal.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN Signal Monitoring: If the sending control unit does not have valid information to send, it may send a defined failure value indicating an invalid signal. Incoming signals with a defined failure value are monitored for signal validity.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the ignition is on for 5 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Controller Area Network - Dedicated Powertrain (CAN-DPT) bus messages not received from the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) for two to five seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If CAN C is still functioning: ESM will continue to communicate over the CAN C bus. Customer will not notice any problems with vehicle. If both CAN DPT and CAN C are not functioning: Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) solenoid will be disabled. (Shifter may be locked in PARK or Neutral.) Gear selection will be disabled. Shift indicator LEDs will be turned on. Shifter background illumination LEDs will be turned off. A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) POWER AND GROUND CIRCUITS</li><li>CAN DPT BUS CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>CAN DPT BUS CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>CAN DPT BUS CIRCUIT SHORTED TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</li><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is this DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the NO RESPONSE FROM ESM (ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE) diagnostic procedure. Refer to NO RESPONSE FROM ESM (ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE) - NAG1 or NO RESPONSE FROM ESM (ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE) 8-SPEED .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS diagnostic procedure. Refer to STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u11e4-00 can communication messages missing\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U11E4-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN COMMUNICATION MESSAGES MISSING</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the diagnostic is to monitor the Controller Area Network (CAN) BUS, the transmitted messages on the CAN BUS and the validity of the CAN signals. Several control units are connected to the CAN bus which send their messages cyclically in a defined time window. The messages contain multiple signals representing vehicle information.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Battery voltage within a valid range. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus monitoring Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. No CAN bus message monitoring DTCs set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The received Data Length Code (DLC) is smaller than the specified length of the message or the content of the message was changed during Transmission.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CAN BUS DTCS PRESENT</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS PRESENT</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to</li><li>PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) BUS DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCS)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any BCM CAN bus DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair BCM CAN bus DTCs. If DTC U0002 is set, perform that diagnostic first. Refer to</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0002-00 can c bus off performance .\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0002-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN C BUS OFF PERFORMANCE .</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any PCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the TCM connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to VALVE BODY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST 8HP45-845RE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1267-00 no valid data from esm on can c or can dpt\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1267-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">NO VALID DATA FROM ESM ON CAN C OR CAN DPT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Transmission Control Module (TCM) monitors the Controller Area Network (CAN) C and CAN DPT circuits for failures. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets when there is a problem with both CAN busses and the TCM can not receive data from the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) to determine the shifter position.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on for a calibrated amount of time. No Controller Area Network (CAN) bus Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. Battery voltage above a calibrated value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">No valid data from Electronic Shift Module (ESM) on CAN C or CAN DPT.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN C (+) CIRCUIT OPEN, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TO VOLTAGE</li><li>CAN C (-) CIRCUIT OPEN, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TO VOLTAGE</li><li>CAN DPT (+) CIRCUIT OPEN, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TO VOLTAGE</li><li>CAN DPT (-) CIRCUIT OPEN, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TO VOLTAGE</li><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to</li><li>PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is this DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the NO RESPONSE FROM ESM (ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE) diagnostic procedure. Refer to NO RESPONSE FROM ESM (ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE) - NAG1 Or NO RESPONSE FROM ESM (ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE) 8-SPEED .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS diagnostic procedure. Refer to STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1400-00 implausible tps signal received\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1400-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE TPS SIGNAL RECEIVED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1401-00 implausible engine speed signal received\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1401-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE ENGINE SPEED SIGNAL RECEIVED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1412-00 implausible vehicle speed signal received\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1412-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE VEHICLE SPEED SIGNAL RECEIVED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1424-00 implausible engine torque signal received\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1424-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE ENGINE TORQUE SIGNAL RECEIVED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1461-00 implausible data received from esm on dpt\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1461-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ESM ON DPT</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ESM ON DPT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1465-00 implausible driver shift request signal received\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1465-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DRIVER SHIFT REQUEST SIGNAL RECEIVED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1466-00 implausible driver shift request signal received on dpt can\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1466-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DRIVER SHIFT REQUEST SIGNAL RECEIVED ON DPT CAN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1467-00 implausible driver shift request signal received on can and dpt can\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1467-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DRIVER SHIFT REQUEST SIGNAL RECEIVED ON CAN AND DPT CAN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1469-00 implausible gear shift position signal sent dpt can\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1469-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE GEAR SHIFT POSITION SIGNAL SENT DPT CAN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1477-00 implausible paddle shifter data received\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1477-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE PADDLE SHIFTER DATA RECEIVED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1479-00 implausible data received from shifter mechanical failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1479-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM SHIFTER MECHANICAL FAILURE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من SHIFTER MECHANICAL FAILURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910399</p></div></div></details></div>";
